-- title:
--   Lipschitz-Gradient Relaxation Bounded By Smooth Relaxation
-- statement:
--   This theorem compares the sequential relaxation generated by globally Lipschitz gradient tests with the smooth-gradient relaxation.
--
--   Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product normed space with its Borel measurable structure and second-countable topology. Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $V$, let $m$ be an additive Haar measure, and let $D$ be a local density for $(\nu,m)$. For every $x\in L^2(\nu)$,
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{sequentialRelaxation}_{\operatorname{lipschitzOperator}(\nu,m,D)}(x)
--   \le
--   \operatorname{relaxation}_{\operatorname{smoothGradient}}(\nu)(x).
--   $$
--
--   The Lean declaration is `lipschitzRelaxation_le_relaxation_readable`. Both sides are `ENNReal`-valued functionals and may equal $\top$. This is an inequality of relaxed energies; it does not assert equality or finiteness.
--
